  "generated_model": "[Abstract Model Plan START]\n1.  **Analyze Query:** The user wants to determine the optimal monthly production quantities for each of 141 explicitly enumerated widgets (Widget1 through Widget141), as well as the amount of CatalystX byproduct from Widget3 to sell (subject to a sales cap and disposal cost for any excess), in order to maximize total profit. The model must respect monthly limits on labor hours, Material A, and Material B.\n2.  **Identify Model Type:** Based on the query, this is a Linear Programming (LP) resource allocation and byproduct management problem.\n3.  **Define Index Sets:** The primary indices are:\n    - Widgets: \\( i \\in \\{\\text{Widget1}, \\text{Widget2}, ..., \\text{Widget141}\\} \\)\n4.  **Define Decision Variables:**\n    -   `x[i]` = Number of units of widget \\( i \\) to produce in the month. Type: GRB.CONTINUOUS (non-negative).\n    -   `s` = Amount (kg) of CatalystX sold in the month. Type: GRB.CONTINUOUS (non-negative).\n    -   `d` = Amount (kg) of CatalystX disposed of in the month. Type: GRB.CONTINUOUS (non-negative).\n5.  **Identify Parameters (from Schema):**\n    -   Objective coefficients:\n        -   Widget profit per unit: from product_resources.csv, column 'Profit' (for each widget).\n        -   CatalystX sale price: $300/kg (given in query).\n        -   CatalystX disposal cost: $200/kg (given in query).\n    -   Constraint coefficients:\n        -   Labor hours per unit: from product_resources.csv, column 'LaborHours'.\n        -   Material A per unit: from product_resources.csv, column 'MaterialA'.\n        -   Material B per unit: from product_resources.csv, column 'MaterialB'.\n        -   CatalystX byproduct rate: 5 kg per unit of Widget3 (given in query).\n    -   Constraint RHS (limits):\n        -   Labor hours: 5,000 (from resource_limits.csv, 'LaborHours').\n        -   Material A: 24,000 kg (from resource_limits.csv, 'MaterialA').\n        -   Material B: 15,000 kg (from resource_limits.csv, 'MaterialB').\n        -   CatalystX sales cap: 1,500 kg/month (from query).\n6.  **Formulate Objective:** Maximize total profit, which is:\n    -   Sum of (profit per unit \u00d7 units produced) for all widgets\n    -   Plus revenue from CatalystX sold (at $300/kg)\n    -   Minus disposal cost for any unsold CatalystX (at $200/kg)\n    -   That is:  \n        Maximize  \n        \\[\n        \\sum_{i=1}^{141} \\text{Profit}[i] \\cdot x[i] + 300 \\cdot s - 200 \\cdot d\n        \\]\n7.  **Formulate Constraints:**\n    -   **Labor Hours Constraint:**  \n        \\[\n        \\sum_{i=1}^{141} \\text{LaborHours}[i] \\cdot x[i] \\leq 5,000\n        \\]\n    -   **Material A Constraint:**  \n        \\[\n        \\sum_{i=1}^{141} \\text{MaterialA}[i] \\cdot x[i] \\leq 24,000\n        \\]\n    -   **Material B Constraint:**  \n        \\[\n        \\sum_{i=1}^{141} \\text{MaterialB}[i] \\cdot x[i] \\leq 15,000\n        \\]\n    -   **CatalystX Mass Balance:**  \n        \\[\n        5 \\cdot x[\\text{Widget3}] = s + d\n        \\]\n        (All CatalystX generated by Widget3 must be either sold or disposed.)\n    -   **CatalystX Sales Cap:**  \n        \\[\n        s \\leq 1,500\n        \\]\n    -   **Non-negativity:**  \n        \\[\n        x[i] \\geq 0 \\quad \\forall i; \\quad s \\geq 0; \\quad d \\geq 0\n        \\]\n[Abstract Model Plan END]",
